## 5. Epic target and story ordering

Parse epic number `N` from user command (e.g. "Work on Epic 3" → `N=3`).

From `sprint-status.yaml` `development_status`:
- Collect keys matching pattern `N-\d+-*` (exclude `epic-*` and `epic-*-retrospective`)
- Filter to status not `done`
- Sort numerically by story number

If `epic-{N}: done` and no incomplete stories → report and stop.

---

## 6. Story loop

Repeat for each story in order. Each phase is a **separate** `agent -p` call. Do not combine phases.

---

### Step 1 — Git branch

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Run these git commands and report the resulting branch name and short SHA:
   BRANCH='dev/epic-{E}-story-{E}-{S}'
   git checkout main && git pull origin main
   git checkout -b \"\${BRANCH}\" 2>/dev/null || git checkout \"\${BRANCH}\""
```

Wait for exit. Confirm branch is `dev/epic-{E}-story-{E}-{S}`.

---

### Step 2 — Create story (only if status is `backlog`)

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Read and execute the full workflow in .cursor/skills/gds-create-story/SKILL.md for story {story-id}.
   Sprint file: _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml.
   Preserve all YAML comments. Update status backlog → ready-for-dev when done."
```

Wait for exit. Verify `{story-id}.md` exists and sprint row is `ready-for-dev`.

> Skip this step if status is already `ready-for-dev` or `in-progress`.

---

### Step 3 — Implement story (status `ready-for-dev` or `in-progress`)

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Read and execute the full workflow in .cursor/skills/gds-dev-story/SKILL.md.
   Story file: _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/{story-id}.md.
   Follow all tasks, run all tests, satisfy Definition of Done.
   Update sprint status to review when complete."
```

Wait for exit. Verify sprint row is `review` and story Status is `review`.

> Skip this step if status is already `review`.

---

### Step 4 — Code review

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Read and execute the full workflow in .cursor/skills/gds-code-review/SKILL.md for story {story-id}.
   Output a triaged findings list (BLOCKER / MAJOR / MINOR)."
```

Wait for exit. Capture all findings.

---

### Step 5 — Fix all review findings (production grade)

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Fix every finding from the code review of story {story-id} with production-quality code.
   No stubs, no TODO comments, no deferred fixes unless the story file explicitly defers with a tracked item.
   Re-run .cursor/skills/gds-dev-story/SKILL.md tasks/subtasks for any structural fix sets."
```

Wait for exit. All findings must be resolved.

---

### Step 6 — Verify (lint / typecheck / tests / build)

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Run the full verification suite for the skribbl project:
   pnpm -r lint && pnpm -r exec tsc --noEmit && pnpm -r test && pnpm -r build
   Fix any failures. Report exit status and any errors."
```

Wait for exit. Must be zero failures before proceeding.

---

### Step 7 — Update status to `done`

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Update _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml:
   Set {story-id} to done. Update last_updated to today. Preserve all YAML comments.
   Also update the Status field in _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/{story-id}.md to done."
```

Wait for exit. Verify both files reflect `done`.

---

### Step 8 — Local commit

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "On branch dev/epic-{E}-story-{E}-{S}, stage and commit all changes:
   git add -A
   git commit -m 'feat({story-id}): <one-line outcome>'
   Do NOT run git push. Report the commit SHA."
```

Wait for exit. Confirm local commit SHA. Do not push.

---

### Step 9 — Next story

If more stories remain (status not `done`) for epic `N`:
- Parse `{E_next}` and `{S_next}` from the next story key
- Go to **Step 1** with the next story's values

If no more stories remain → proceed to **§7 Epic completion**.

---

## 7. Epic completion

Run as one blocking `agent -p` call:

```bash
agent -p --workspace "/Users/mac/Desktop/femil/skribbl" --output-format json \
  "Epic {N} is complete. Do the following in order:
   1. Set epic-{N} to done in _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml. Preserve all comments.
   2. Write _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/epic-{N}-complete.md with:
      - Story table (story-id, branch, status)
      - Epic AC coverage mapped from _bmad-output/planning-artifacts/epics.md
      - Deferred items
      - Next backlog epic from sprint file
   3. git add -A && git commit -m 'docs(epic-{N}): epic complete summary and sprint closure'
   4. Do NOT git push.
   5. Print list of all dev/epic-{N}-story-* branches and their HEAD SHAs."
```

Wait for exit. Then **STOP** — do not start the next epic. Tell the user:
- All branches and SHAs for this epic
- "Local history ready for manual review. Run 'Work on Epic {N+1}' when ready."

---

## 8. Rules

- **Cursor CLI always**: every step uses `agent -p --workspace ... --output-format json`. No exceptions.
- **One step at a time**: wait for each `agent -p` process to exit before the next.
- **BLOCKED**: if any step fails or is ambiguous, state `BLOCKED: {reason}` and stop.
- **Status order**: `backlog → ready-for-dev → in-progress → review → done`. Never skip or reverse.
- **`done` only after Step 6 is green**: status update (Step 7) is always last before commit.
- **Branch**: always `dev/epic-{E}-story-{E}-{S}`. Never `feature/`.
- **No push**: local commits only until human approves.
- **No scope creep**: implement only what story ACs require.
- **Context7**: use for any library/CLI doc lookup (`resolve-library-id` → `query-docs`).
